across the periodic boundary. The stacking sequence within the wurtzite unit cell creates dimer layers that are shifted in the x-direction. With an odd number of dimer layers, the periodic boundary condition forces the top 'A' layer to connect with the bottom 'A' layer instead of the expected 'B' layer, leading to the defect. This connection introduces an antiphase boundary that significantly alters the energy of the system.\n\n\nThe odd-N bulk calculations are definitively flawed by an antiphase boundary with approximately 36 eV excess energy. This defect arises because the periodic boundary condition forces an incorrect stacking sequence, adding a stacking fault to the wurtzite unit cell. This boundary correction explains the discrepancies in calculated bulk energies and, consequently, the erroneous surface energy values. Verifying this, the lattice vector calculations confirm that the bulk crystallographic period along $[10\\bar{1}0]$ is equivalent to two dimer layers.\n\n\nThe lattice vector analysis confirms that in 2H-SiC bulk, an odd number of dimer layers necessarily introduces an antiphase boundary (APB) defect. This is because the periodic boundary conditions force an incorrect stacking sequence, unlike in slab calculations where surfaces are free and do not wrap. Comparing even and odd periods confirms the constant bulk energy per atom in the even-layer systems. The bulk energy is $-443.4935\\text{ eV/atom}$. This analysis confirms that the odd-N systems are flawed due to the APB defect.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"/home/WORKSTATION4WSL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/mdi_env_rtx5080/bin/python3 -c \\\"\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\nAREA_2A = 279.497664\\nCONV_FACTOR = 16.021766\\nEFFECTIVE_DENOM = AREA_2A / CONV_FACTOR\\n\\n# Reference bulk energy per atom from 10 periods true bulk SCF\\ne_bulk_per_atom = -159657.6701 / 360.0 # -443.493528 eV/atom\\n\\nslab_energies = {\\n    1: -15945.0989,\\n    2: -31892.6430,\\n    3: -47856.6115,\\n    4: -63822.0658,\\n    5: -79787.7398,\\n    6: -95753.5368,\\n    7: -111719.3218,\\n    8: -127685.0579,\\n    9: -143650.8317,\\n    10: -159616.6027\\n}\\n\\nprint('Period | Natoms | E_slab (eV) | E_bulk_true (eV) | Delta_E (eV) | Gamma (J/m^2)')\\nprint('-----------------------------------------------------------------------------')\\nfor n in range(1, 11):\\n    natoms = 36 * n\\n    eslab = slab_energies[n]\\n    ebulk = natoms * e_bulk_per_atom\\n    de = eslab - ebulk\\n    gamma = de / EFFECTIVE_DENOM\\n    print(f'{n:6d} | {natoms:6d} | {eslab:11.4f} | {ebulk:16.4f} | {de:12.4f} | {gamma:13.4f}')\\n\\\"\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolSummary":"\"Calculate surface energy with true bulk energy per atom\""}}]}
